<h2>
What Does QR Code Mean?
</h2>


<p>
A QR code is a two-dimensional digital barcode that stores information and provides instant access to digital content by scanning it through a mobile device.
</p>


<p>
Unlike traditional barcodes, QR codes can store more information and provide access to websites, payments, digital menus, and other online resources. Brands use QR codes on product packaging to provide additional information, instructions, reviews, and promotions. Restaurants also use QR codes for digital menus, allowing customers to access menus through smartphones.
</p>





